 true, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"src_outgoing_trim_doc\"}, {\"object\": \"interpretations\", \"action\": \"append\", \"target\": \"interpretations[0]\", \"investigation_id\": \"9527b916ba184b74865563c980642d1c-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"experiment_id\", \"source_ids\", \"executions\", \"conclusion\", \"rationale\", \"limitations\"]}, {\"object\": \"experiments\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"experiment\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Closed the event-backpressure question as a supported defect: the revised execution (ff4511e8f6684444b8b1ec403335f9f8, exit 0, both tests passed, no parsing errors) now carries the operands, so the interpretation cites parsed events 2/3/4 (all three event channels full at capacity 64, node 1's actor parked across ten 200ms samples, its append_notify endpoint withheld after 4s though its deadline is 300ms) against control events 0/1 (same cluster with drained streams: all nodes answering, follower append_notify Ok(idx 2)), conclusion holds with defect_claim asserted and the node-local/capacity limits kept. Also requested the first core probe for execution: a deterministic 2-node in-process simulation (omnipaxos package, draft core_lost_accepted.rs) that elects node 1, appends one entry, discards exactly the follower's Accepted, runs 100 resend periods with everything else delivered and asserts no decision with both nodes holding the entry, then shows a later unrelated proposal is what repairs it; the delivered-receipt control runs in the same execution. That harness could not be locally verified this turn because building the omnipaxos test target's dev-dependencies (kompact and friends) exceeded my local build window; the executed receipt will settle it.\"}"}}
